\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Schematic illustration of the TCV-$\phi $ linear matter power spectrum at $z=0$. The solid curve is the CLASS cold--dark--matter spectrum $P_{\rm  cdm}(k)$ for the effective parameter set~\eqref  {eq:theta-tcv}; the dashed curve shows the fuzzy--DM--modified spectrum $P_{\rm  eff}(k)=T_{\rm  F}^2(k)P_{\rm  cdm}(k)$ with $k_J=5\,h\,\mathrm  {Mpc}^{-1}$ and $n=4$. Within this phenomenological template, the resulting illustrative spectrum $P_{\rm  eff}(k)$ coincides with $\Lambda $CDM on large scales and exhibits an ULDM--like suppression at small scales. }}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:Pk_fuzzy}{{2}{7}{Schematic illustration of the TCV-$\phi $ linear matter power spectrum at $z=0$. The solid curve is the CLASS cold--dark--matter spectrum $P_{\rm cdm}(k)$ for the effective parameter set~\eqref {eq:theta-tcv}; the dashed curve shows the fuzzy--DM--modified spectrum $P_{\rm eff}(k)=T_{\rm F}^2(k)P_{\rm cdm}(k)$ with $k_J=5\,h\,\mathrm {Mpc}^{-1}$ and $n=4$. Within this phenomenological template, the resulting illustrative spectrum $P_{\rm eff}(k)$ coincides with $\Lambda $CDM on large scales and exhibits an ULDM--like suppression at small scales}{figure.2}{}}
